// BASE LIFE (owner Nov 17 16:01 "quite bare", 16:02 "and only 2 house", 16:03 "additional house when recruit come in"): the villagers' houses, the recruits' plots and houses,
// the lived-in set pieces and the lanes, plus the entry that builds the water (src/basewater.js). Layout and rules: src/baselife.js; numbers: CONFIG.baseLife (high = desktop, low = phones).
// Houses are the base's own style (plaster walls on a stone plinth, a barrel vault that is a garden, round windows with copper frames, an arched door), closed and not entered: warm light and
// curtains in the windows. Each differs (size, roof, colours, porch / lean-to / panels / lookout) and is lived in outside (window boxes, rain barrel with a downpipe, lantern, bench, laundry,
// nameplate, the owner's tools or hobby). A recruit's plot: stakes and string on cleared ground; the day they join a timber frame with scaffolding; from the next day a finished house.
